New vacuity class, found while establishing what is on the firmware
webauthn branch. Every prior instance was inside a single tree; this one
is a property of branch topology and nothing checks it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NqivnLpopLHdyL62k5JaJx
---
 AGENTS.md | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index e029cac..4453fa8 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -75,6 +75,16 @@ device-trust core.
     Written as one undifferentiated "partial", the verifiable half gets
     re-litigated by whoever reads it next.
 
+12. **A guard and the thing it guards must live on the same branch.** Otherwise
+    the guard is vacuous, and vacuous in the direction that reads as a pass. On
+    the firmware side,
+    `test_attest__the_reference_credential_store_is_empty` guards
+    `configs/kvmd/webauthn.json`, which exists on only one branch — so on every
+    other branch the guard skips and certifies nothing. Every prior vacuity was
+    inside a single tree; this class is a property of the branch topology, and
+    nothing checks it. Before trusting a guard, confirm its subject is present
+    on the branch you are on.
+
 ## Where to look
 - `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — core + modules, the boundary, the connection swap.
 - `docs/DECISIONS.md` — settled calls; read before proposing a change to one.
